    <switch x="500" y="10" height="40" on="false" variable="symmetric-information?" width="181" display="symmetric-information?"></switch>
    <switch x="692" y="489" height="60" on="false" variable="government?" width="112" display="government?"></switch>
    <button x="426" y="63" height="40" disableUntilTicks="false" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="65" display="go once">go</button>
    <button x="373" y="14" height="40" disableUntilTicks="false" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="89">setup</button>
    <button x="335" y="62" height="40" disableUntilTicks="true" forever="true" kind="Observer" width="85">go</button>
    <slider x="164" step="1" y="59" max="100" width="168" display="lucky-percentage" height="50" min="0" direction="Horizontal" default="28.0" variable="lucky-percentage" units="%"></slider>
    <switch x="5" y="59" height="50" on="true" variable="insurance-market?" width="158" display="insurance-market?"></switch>
    <slider x="38" step="50" y="6" max="2000" width="250" display="n-consumers" height="50" min="50" direction="Horizontal" default="1000.0" variable="n-consumers"></slider>
  </widgets>
  <info># Insurance ABM Model

This model simulates an insurance market with heterogeneous agents, adverse selection, insurer capital constraints, government subsidies, and pricing strategies.

This version of the model was presented at the 1st Brazilian Interdisciplinary Symposium on Agent-Based Models – São Paulo, May 28, 2026.

Developed in NetLogo.

André Ferreira Santos 
Universidade de Brasília 
Maio - 2026 </info>
